/Alt (The flowchart illustrates the RBC-AD framework, detailing its components and flow. It begins with a Predictive Model, which uses Causal Dilated TCN. This model connects to Calibration and Thresholding, which includes Calibration Split, Conformal Quantiles, FAR-Controlled Threshold, and Alarm Limit. Separately, a Frequency Feature Bank performs FFT Analysis and feeds into a Scoring Module, which calculates Gaussian NLL Score and Frequency Deviation Score. These scores are combined into a Fused Detection Score alpha times NLL plus 1 minus alpha times FD. This fused score then enters a Three-State Decision Logic, categorising outcomes as Normal, Uncertain, or Anomaly, corresponding to SAFE, UNC&#132;E&#132;R&#132;T&#132;AIN, and ALERT states. The decision logic leads to Deployment and Inference, which involves Sliding Window Inference and k-Consecutive Alarms. Deployment and Inference also connects to Root Cause Attribution, which performs Per-Feature NLL Analysis and Ranked Variable Reporting. An Evaluation Protocol at the bottom assesses FAR Compliance, Uncertainty Rate, and Detection Delay.)
/K 8
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
