/A 2554 0 R
/Alt (The two-panel graph shows ROC and PR curves for TEP fault detection. Panel a, titled ROC Curve - TEP Fault Detection, displays a line graph with False Positive Rate on the horizontal axis from 0.0 to 1.0 and True Positive Rate on the vertical axis from 0.0 to 1.0. The ROC curve, labelled ROC curve AUC equals 1.0000, is an orange line that rises sharply from 0.0 False Positive Rate to 1.0 True Positive Rate, then remains flat at 1.0 True Positive Rate across the rest of the horizontal axis. A dashed black line extends diagonally from 0.0, 0.0 to 1.0, 1.0. Panel b, titled Precision-Recall Curve - TEP Fault Detection, displays a line graph with Recall on the horizontal axis from 0.0 to 1.0 and Precision on the vertical axis from 0.75 to 1.00. The PR curve, labelled PR curve AUC equals 1.0000, is a blue line that remains flat at 1.00 Precision across the entire horizontal axis from 0.0 to 1.0 Recall.)
/K 104
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 22 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
